@startuml
title Defense Core — In-Memory Choreography Sequence
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Workflow operator" as Operator
participant "FastAPI boundary" as Boundary
participant "Application service" as Service
participant "Definition validator" as Validator
participant "Choreography strategy" as Choreography
participant "Run-scoped in-memory\nEventBus" as EventBus
participant "Controlled workflow-advance\nhandler (one per run)" as Handler
participant "Deterministic scenario" as Scenario
participant "Shared retry /\ntransition resolver" as Resolver
participant "Persistence boundary" as Persistence
database "Persistent database" as Database

Operator -> Boundary : start workflow candidate\nwith choreography + named scenario
Boundary -> Service : request run
Service -> Validator : validate complete definition

alt definition invalid
  Validator --> Service : rejected with violations
  Service --> Boundary : rejection; no run identity
  Boundary --> Operator : validation feedback
  note over Service,Database
  No run or execution state is created.
  No EventBus subscription is created.
  end note
else definition accepted
  Validator --> Service : accepted definition
  Service -> Persistence : create isolated run + initial trace
  Persistence -> Database : commit run state
  Database --> Persistence : committed
  Service -> Choreography : execute(run, definition, scenario)
  Choreography -> EventBus : subscribe run channel to Handler
  Choreography -> Handler : begin with designated start task

  loop deterministic run advancement until terminal
    Handler -> Scenario : next deterministic outcome(task)
    Scenario --> Handler : SUCCESS or FAILURE
    Handler -> Persistence : persist attempt ordinal + outcome
    Persistence -> Database : commit ordered attempt trace
    Database --> Persistence : committed

    alt FAILURE and completed attempts below bound
      Handler -> Persistence : persist retry observation
      Persistence -> Database : commit ordered retry trace
      Database --> Persistence : committed
      Handler -> EventBus : publish same-task retry event for this run
      EventBus -> Handler : synchronous ordered dispatch
      note over Handler,EventBus
      Retry does not select or traverse a graph edge.
      end note
    else final outcome or attempt bound reached
      Handler -> Resolver : resolve final outcome + outgoing transitions
      note over Handler,Resolver
      SUCCESS / FAILURE precedes ALWAYS.
      At exhaustion, final FAILURE is resolved normally.
      end note
      alt eligible transition selected
        Resolver --> Handler : next task + selected transition
        Handler -> Persistence : persist transition selection
        Persistence -> Database : commit before event publication
        Database --> Persistence : committed
        Handler -> EventBus : publish next-task event for this run
        EventBus -> Handler : synchronous ordered dispatch
      else no eligible transition after SUCCESS
        Resolver --> Handler : successful terminal
        Handler -> Persistence : persist successful terminal + trace
        Persistence -> Database : commit together
        Database --> Persistence : committed
        Handler -> EventBus : signal terminal cleanup
      else no eligible transition after FAILURE
        Resolver --> Handler : unsuccessful terminal
        Handler -> Persistence : persist unsuccessful terminal + trace
        Persistence -> Database : commit together
        Database --> Persistence : committed
        Handler -> EventBus : signal terminal cleanup
      end
    end
  end

  Choreography -> EventBus : unsubscribe Handler and clear run channel
  Choreography --> Service : terminal run result
  Service --> Boundary : run identity, status, trace reference
  Boundary --> Operator : inspect persistent ordered trace
end

note bottom of EventBus
In-memory only; one controlled advance handler per run.
No business dependence on unrelated subscriber order.
No Kafka, ZooKeeper, broker, or broker fallback.
end note

legend
Status: APPROVED — checkpoint 4 architecture baseline
Requirements baseline: 6074fd7ef490ea3b08177e7a786035159f39a91c
Working base: b5c7da9e51382bb418f017790ae944c8dff26a06
Implementation: NOT STARTED
Executable verification: NOT STARTED
Release: NOT SCHEDULED
Sequence is accepted checkpoint-4 design behavior, not an executed or passed case.
endlegend
@enduml
